# Grid paths in the mixin encoding of inheritance
# (corpora/contest_mixin_library.pl, the libraries `natural` and `binary`):
# problems of the reduction series, ported from the
# retired labeled points of contest_inheritance_dynamic.pl and
# contest_inheritance_dynamic_middle.pl.
#
# THE PROBLEM. The number of monotone lattice paths from (i, j) to (0, 0)
# is paths(i, j) = 1 when i = 0 or j = 0, and paths(i - 1, j) +
# paths(i, j - 1) otherwise, which is C(i + j, i). The class grid has the
# slots i, j (unary naturals) and count (a binary natural), and is the one
# slot of a module of width 1, so that count makes objects of the class
# read through the module's self. count dispatches on self.i's and
# self.j's accept, and answers up.count.plus(left.count) with
# up = {grid, i : self.i.predecessor, j : self.j} and
# left = {grid, i : self.i, j : self.j.predecessor}. The two calls
# reach paths(i - 1, j - 1) by different spellings, so a reading that
# shares only equal spellings makes about C(2n, n) calls, 4 a step of n;
# the reference (contest_dynamic_references:reference_grid_paths/3) is the
# usual table, O(n^2) additions.
#
# THE PROGRAM reads C.equality({grid, i : n, j : n}.count) at church,
# the labeled program's check: paths(n, n) for n = 2 .. 8, and the wrong
# paths(4, 4) == 134, off by 2^6 in a high bit.
#
# THE SNAPSHOT of each is the Boolean of the equation. PROOF:
# the recursion descends on the finite unary numerals under every choice,
# every class has one implementation of each slot it is read at, and every
# end is the Boolean of the equation.
#
# LIMITS: the family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.

#   grid_point(?Point, ?Size, ?Claimed)
#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "integer") "cbor")
λ integer_from_cbor _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. integer_from_cbor λx. x)
λ integer
. export
λ
. cons (λ_grid_point. _grid_point (text "reduction_mixin_grid_paths_two") (integer 2) λ. integer 6)
λ
. cons (λ_grid_point. _grid_point (text "reduction_mixin_grid_paths_three") (integer 3) λ. integer 20)
λ
. cons (λ_grid_point. _grid_point (text "reduction_mixin_grid_paths_four") (integer 4) λ. integer 70)
λ
